# Target C: Profile B distinguished touch-three kernel split

Date: 2026-09-22

Status: rigorous necessary strengthening of the remaining eight-no-root `k=6,D=-1,p=9` Profile B. This note does not close Profile B. It identifies the exact source-basis position of the one internal kernel direction in the forced `d_5=2` puncture and turns that identity into a new source-level filter.

Companion verifier:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_touch3_kernel_witness_2026_09_22.py`

The two inputs are already proved in the repository.

1. The touch-four-alternative closure proves that every genuine remaining Profile B source has a chosen singleton block `b` which is aligned, dependency-active, and touched by exactly three source cycles. If `T` is that three-coordinate touch set, deleting `T` preserves coefficient rank two and gives a five-row virtual-canonical descendant of deficiency

```text
d_5=2.
```

2. The exact kernel-lattice theorem fixes the nine chosen source singleton replacement classes as a basis of the nine-dimensional source quotient `V_8`. In those basis coordinates, write

```text
q_1,...,q_9
```

for the source basis and identify them with the standard coordinate vectors of `Q^9`. Let `L=W^perp` be the six-dimensional external subspace generated by the kernels of the rank-preserving `d=3` punctures. For a clean triple deletion `T`, let

```text
E_T <= L
```

be the three-dimensional external kernel span generated by the three corresponding one-coordinate puncture kernel lines, and let

```text
K_T = ker(V_8 -> V_5(T)).
```

When the five-row child has `d_5=2`, the exact kernel-lattice theorem gives

```text
dim K_T = 4,
E_T <= K_T,
K_T intersect L = E_T.
```

Because the coefficient minimum distance is at least four, all eight source coordinates are three-clean, so the forced touch triple is represented in the existing all-clean fan.

## 1. Distinguished kernel-splitting lemma

Let `b=q_j` be the dependency-active aligned singleton block supplied by the touch-four-alternative closure, and let `T` be its three source touches.

Dependency-active means precisely

```text
q_j notin L.                                      (1.1)
```

Deleting all three coordinates in `T` makes `b` untouched. Therefore its source replacement class maps to zero in the five-row descendant, so

```text
q_j in K_T.                                       (1.2)
```

Since `E_T <= L`, (1.1) implies `q_j notin E_T`. Hence

```text
dim span(E_T,q_j)=4.
```

But `K_T` is four-dimensional and contains both `E_T` and `q_j`. Therefore

```text
K_T = E_T direct-sum <q_j>.                       (1.3)
```

This is stronger than the previously imposed `d_5=2` kernel condition. The earlier exact kernel-lattice audit required only that a `d_5=2` kernel be four-dimensional, contain the three-dimensional external span, and meet `L` exactly in that external span. It did not require the remaining one-dimensional kernel direction to be represented by the coordinate basis class of an actual aligned touch-three source singleton block.

## 2. Source-level necessary filter

For each chosen nine-block source basis, the new verifier reconstructs the complete puncture-kernel lattice and computes

```text
L = span(all d=3 puncture kernels).
```

It then scans the nine chosen source blocks. A block is a candidate witness only if all of the following hold exactly:

1. its local empty constraint has rank one, so it is aligned;
2. its source basis vector `q_j` is not contained in `L`, so it is dependency-active;
3. exactly three selected source cycles touch the block;
4. deleting those three source coordinates has rank-two coefficient space and virtual deficiency `d_5=2`;
5. `q_j` lies in the resulting four-dimensional puncture kernel;
6. if `E_T` is the span of the three one-puncture kernel lines for those deleted coordinates, then

```text
K_T = span(E_T,q_j).
```

A genuine Profile B source must contain at least one such witness.

The test is exact rational linear algebra. It is only a necessary filter: failure rejects a source basis rigorously; passing does not prove realizability.

## 3. Distinct witnesses give distinct deletion triples

There is also a small geometric corollary. An aligned touch-three block has its three source touches inside one aligned four-cycle direction star. Two distinct aligned stars intersect in at most one global no-root cycle. Therefore two distinct aligned touch-three blocks cannot have the same three-coordinate touch set.

Thus every distinct active aligned touch-three witness gives a distinct forced `d_5=2` triple puncture. This may become useful if later counting forces more than one active aligned block.

## 4. Computational status

The companion wrapper is implemented on top of the exact kernel-lattice audit. It preserves all previous filters and adds the witness test only after the existing exact kernel-lattice conditions pass.

The new wrapper was syntax-checked locally with `python -m py_compile`. The full repository census was not executed in this run, so no survivor count and no Profile B closure are claimed here.

The next target is to run this filter on the remaining source cover or, if execution remains expensive, derive further restrictions from the coordinate-split identity (1.3), especially on how the distinguished source coordinate can sit relative to the other active basis classes modulo `L`.